<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31057" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nixor</span></b> , āri, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>dep. n.</i> [1. nitor], <i>to lean</i> or <i>rest upon; to
				strive, endeavor</i> (<b>poet.</b>).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 6,
			836</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3,
			1001</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pars vulnere clauda retentat Nixantem
					(serpentem),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 5, 279</span></i>
			 Wagner <i>N. cr.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to depend upon</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundamenta, quibus nixatur vita salusque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					4, 506</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
